      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nAn exceptional equestrian property with the residence extending to approx. 339 sqm and with impressive equine facilities set on approximately 7.9 acres of quality land with stable block, equine yard and extensive road frontage.\n\nThe home itself is wonderfully spacious and bright and gives a hearty welcome from the moment you step inside. \n\nIt spans over approx. 339 sqm. with four reception rooms, four bedrooms, four bathrooms, office and many more besides.\n\nThe property is approached by a tree lined tarmacadam driveway set amidst beautifully maintained grounds which are mainly laid out in lawn and bordered by a selection of mature trees and hedging. \n\nTo the rear of the property there is a fenced hardcore tennis court, haybarn, stable block sheds, enhancing the rural charm of the setting.\n\nDesigned with the equestrian enthusiast in mind, the property benefits from excellent facilities suitable for private use, training or boutique equestrian operations.\n\nThis attractive setting provides a private and peaceful oasis away from the hustle and bustle, while still offering immediate access to the excellent amenities of the town. \n\nThis elegant home offers the perfect blend of quality craftsmanship, spacious design, and energy efficiency.\n\nThis wonderful home exudes exquisite taste and is further enhanced by a host of attractive features and finishes throughout ensuring that this is a home that will impress even the most discerning purchaser.\n\nThe well-appointed kitchen with island unit and granite worktop forms the heart of the home with step down access to the split level family room with stove, double doors to rear patio and access also to the adjoining large living room and sunroom.\n\nRarely does such a substantial home come to the market so close to the town centre, offering the ideal balance of peaceful seclusion and everyday convenience. \n\nHoganswood is a sought after location due to its attractive, rustic yet convenient setting close to Clane village where you can avail of excellent shops, schools, church, cafes, restaurants, pubs, leisure centre and an array of sporting and recreational facilities. \nCommuting to Dublin city and its surrounding areas could not be easier via a frequent bus service, rail links from nearby Sallins and Maynooth combined with proximity to the M4 and M7 motorways."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nReception Hall - 3.7 x 3.05\nWith solid wood flooring, decorative wood wall panelling, coved ceiling, lightfittings.\n\nKitchen Dining Room - 7.55 x 6.55\nWith fitted kitchen, tiled flooring, coved ceiling, recessed lighting, breakfast island, American style fridge, AGA cast-iron heat storage oven, wine cooler, double oven, microwave, classic flooring, double doors to dining room, built in display and storage cabinets, split level step down to family room.\n\nFamily Room - 5.6 x 4.35\nStepped down from kitchen with coved ceiling, recessed lighting, dual aspect, double doors to rear patio area, feature firesurround with solid fuel stove insert, double window seats and double doors to living room.\n\nLiving Room - 7.4 x 5.6\nLarge bright room with coved ceiling, recessed lighting, dual aspect with feature fireplace, cast iron spiral staircase to attic rooms, access to sunroom and steps up to dining room.\n\nSun Room - 4.15 x 3.7\nWith tiled flooring, roof blinds, light fitting, double doors to living room.\n\nDining Room - 4.9 x 3.85\nBeautiful bright room overlooking the font gardens with double doors to kitchen and step down split level steps to living room.\n\nOffice / Reception Room - 4.4 x 3.60\nDual aspect room to front with feature fireplace, built in shelving and desk, large picture window, coved ceiling.\n\nBathroom - 2.6 x 1.65\nWith bath, Triton electric shower over the bath, shower screen, vanity whb, wc, tiled floor, tiled walls, mirror.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.6 x 2.25\nTo front with coved ceiling.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.5 x 6\nTo rear with coved ceiling, wardrobe /dressing area with archway to bedroom area.\n\nMaster Bedroom - 4.7 x 4.35\nLarge room comprising bedroom area, large en-suite bathroom and walk in closet room.\n\nEn-Suite - 4.35 x 2.6\nFull sized en-suite bathroom with three piece bathroom suite, coved ceiling, tiled floor , extractor fan, double sink and cabinet, shower unit, access to walk in closet room.\n\nWalk In Closet - 4.35 x 3.4\nWith wood flooring, recessed lighting, extensive wardrobe and storage closets.\n\nAttic Room 1 - 5.5 x 4.6\nLarge spacious room with wardrobes, dressing table, ensuite bathroom and large attic room off.\n\nEn-Suite - 16.5 x 1.6\nFully tiled with shower unit, w.c., w.h.b., Velux window.\n\nAttic Room 2 - 5.8 x 3.65\nLarge room with wardrobes, storage, recessed lights and large window.\n\nUtility / Laundry Room - 3.8 x 2.65\nExtensive storage wall and base units, tiled floor, sink unit, plumbed for appliances.\n\nBack Hall - 2.5 x 2.45\nWith tiled floor, storage units\n\nBack Hall Closet - 3.4 x 1.65\n\n\nGuest W.C. - 2.5 x 2.45\nWith tiled floor, w.c. & w.h.b.\n\nSpecial Features & Services - \nStable Block with 6 stables.Large haybarnWell-fenced paddocks laid out in 2 manageable divisions Excellent grazing land suitable for any agricultural or equestrian useFenced tennis courtPatio and seating areasBeautiful mature lawns and gardensMature gardens and extensive outdoor entertaining space Large gated tree lined avenue and electric entrance gatesMains water, private septic tankBroadband availableSuperb educational, recreational and shopping facilities close byIncluded: kitchen & utility appliances.Mains water, private septic tank.\n\n"
